  "content": {
    "id": "v2-481a5-p20-practice-slot-11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "The line $ax + by - 6 = 0$ is perpendicular to $2x - 5y = 1$ and passes through $(-1,4)$.\nFind the values of $a$ and $b$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=10,\\quad b=4$.",
      "worked": "The original gradient is $\\dfrac{2}{5}$, so the perpendicular gradient is $-\\dfrac{5}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y-4&=-\\frac{5}{2}(x+1)\\\\2y-8&=-5x-5\\\\5x+2y-3&=0\\end{align*}$$\nThe constant term must be $-6$, so multiply by $2$: $10x+4y-6=0$.\nComparing with $ax+by-6=0$ gives $a=10$ and $b=4$. Check: $10(-1)+4(4)-6=0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
